---
// Experience, projects, education & skills — departures board
---
<section id="experience" class="poster" aria-label="Experience, projects, education and skills">
  <div class="band"><p class="band-label" data-i18n="xp.kicker">02 / EXPERIENCE — SYSTEM HISTORY</p></div>
  <div class="sheet">
    <h2 class="stops">
      <span>Story</span><span>Code</span><span>System</span><span>Security</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="rows">
      <article class="row job now">
        <p class="when" data-i18n="xp.j1.when">FEB 2026 — JUL 2026</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4 data-i18n="xp.j1.role">Junior Developer · Security Engineering</h4>
          <p class="org">Overside Srl</p>
          <p data-i18n="xp.j1.desc">I built Overguard, a platform that helps small businesses spot phishing emails and Business Email Compromise fraud. It was also my ITS thesis project.</p>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.did">What I did</p>
          <ul class="points" data-i18n="xp.j1.points">
            <li>Automated analysis of email headers, sender, domain and links, with extraction of indicators of compromise (IoCs).</li>
            <li>Risk scoring across 5 threat intelligence sources (VirusTotal, AlienVault OTX, URLScan.io, Hybrid Analysis, Google Safe Browsing), with caching and fallback when a source doesn't respond.</li>
            <li>DLP module that checks outgoing emails for sensitive content.</li>
            <li>.NET 10 backend with JWT-secured REST APIs, PostgreSQL and Docker deployment on Linux; Chrome and Thunderbird extensions connected to the backend.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.learned">What I learned</p>
          <p data-i18n="xp.j1.learn">How to design a complete system, from the database to the browser extensions, and to ask early on what can go wrong: a source that stops responding, an API rate limit, data leaving when it shouldn't.</p>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.stack">Stack</p>
          <ul class="run">
            <li>C#</li><li>.NET 10</li><li>ASP.NET Core</li><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>REST API</li>
            <li>JWT</li><li>Docker</li><li>Linux</li><li>Git</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="row job">
        <p class="when" data-i18n="xp.j2.when">APR 2025 — JAN 2026</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4 data-i18n="xp.j2.role">Junior Developer</h4>
          <p class="org">Levante Yachts Srl</p>
          <p data-i18n="xp.j2.desc">I worked on the company portal, on both frontend and backend.</p>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.did">What I did</p>
          <ul class="points" data-i18n="xp.j2.points">
            <li>Automated content publishing by connecting WordPress and Google Sheets through REST APIs.</li>
            <li>Managed the MySQL database, writing SQL queries to verify and clean data.</li>
            <li>Built pages and features in HTML, CSS, JavaScript and PHP.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.learned">What I learned</p>
          <p data-i18n="xp.j2.learn">How to work on a live system, where every change touches real data and content.</p>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.stack">Stack</p>
          <ul class="run">
            <li>HTML</li><li>CSS</li><li>JavaScript</li><li>PHP</li><li>MySQL</li>
            <li>WordPress API</li><li>Google Sheets API</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="sub-title" data-i18n="proj.title">Projects</h3>
    <div class="rows">
      <article class="row job">
        <p class="when">2026</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4 data-i18n="proj.p1.title">This portfolio</h4>
          <p class="org">Astro · Netlify</p>
          <p data-i18n="proj.p1.desc">The site you're reading: I built it with security as the starting point, not an add-on.</p>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.did">What I did</p>
          <ul class="points" data-i18n="proj.p1.points">
            <li>Static site, to keep the attack surface as small as possible.</li>
            <li>HTTP security headers (CSP, HSTS, Permissions-Policy), rated A+ on securityheaders.com.</li>
            <li>Code scanning with Semgrep and custom rules, dependency checks with npm audit.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="run-label" data-i18n="xp.learned">What I learned</p>
          <p data-i18n="proj.p1.learn">To apply what I'd studied to a project of my own: hardening, static analysis and triaging the findings.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="sub-title" data-i18n="edu.title">Education &amp; Certifications</h3>
    <div class="rows">
      <article class="row edu">
        <p class="when" data-i18n="edu.e4.when">IN PROGRESS — 2026</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4>CEH — Certified Ethical Hacker</h4>
          <p class="org">EC-Council</p>
          <p data-i18n="edu.e4.desc">Currently preparing: ethical hacking, vulnerabilities, network and system security.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="row edu">
        <p class="when">2024 — 2026</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4>ITS Smart Academy</h4>
          <p class="org" data-i18n="edu.e1.sub">INDUSTRIAL SOFTWARE DEVELOPER<br>EQF LEVEL 5 · 110/110 CUM LAUDE</p>
          <p data-i18n="edu.e1.desc">Two-year higher technical program in industrial software development.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="row edu">
        <p class="when">2024</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4>Università Politecnica delle Marche</h4>
          <p class="org">Cyber Risk &amp; Data Protection</p>
          <p data-i18n="edu.e2.desc">Postgraduate course (25 ECTS): GDPR, risk management, network and software security.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="row edu">
        <p class="when">2024</p>
        <div class="body">
          <h4>Google Cybersecurity Certificate</h4>
          <p class="org">Foundations &amp; Operations</p>
          <p data-i18n="edu.e3.desc">Python, Linux, SQL, SIEM, IDS, risk assessment, threat identification, security controls.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="sub-title" data-i18n="skills.title">Skills</h3>
    <div class="rows skills">
      <div class="row" role="group" aria-labelledby="sk-dev">
        <h4 id="sk-dev" data-i18n="skills.dev">Development</h4>
        <ul class="run">
          <li>C#</li><li>.NET 10</li><li>ASP.NET Core</li><li>Entity Framework</li><li>JavaScript</li>
          <li>PHP</li><li>Python</li><li>Flutter</li><li>SQL</li><li>PostgreSQL</li><li>MySQL</li><li>Git</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="row" role="group" aria-labelledby="sk-cyber">
        <h4 id="sk-cyber" data-i18n="skills.cyber">Cybersecurity</h4>
        <ul class="run strong">
          <li>Phishing &amp; BEC detection</li><li>Threat intelligence</li><li>IoC correlation</li>
          <li>Risk scoring</li><li>DLP</li><li>HTTP hardening</li><li>SAST / SCA</li>
          <li>Log analysis</li><li>Risk assessment</li><li>GDPR</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="row" role="group" aria-labelledby="sk-tools">
        <h4 id="sk-tools" data-i18n="skills.tools">Tools &amp; Infrastructure</h4>
        <ul class="run">
          <li>Linux</li><li>Bash</li><li>Docker</li><li>REST API</li><li>JWT</li><li>Semgrep</li><li>npm audit</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="row" role="group" aria-labelledby="sk-human">
        <h4 id="sk-human" data-i18n="skills.human">Soft skills</h4>
        <ul class="run" data-i18n="skills.human.list">
          <li>Analytical thinking</li><li>Problem solving</li><li>Attention to detail</li>
          <li>Technical documentation</li><li>Independent project ownership</li><li>Clear communication</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
